  "question": {
    "text": "If the area of the region<br/>$\\left\\{(x, y):\\left|4-x^2\\right| \\leq y \\leq x^2, y \\leq 4, x \\geq 0\\right\\}$<br/>is $\\left(\\frac{80 \\sqrt{2}}{\\alpha}-\\beta\\right), \\boldsymbol{\\alpha}, \\boldsymbol{\\beta} \\in \\mathbf{N}$, then $\\alpha+\\beta$ is equal to _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "22",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1OsYtCfd5SMFGJbgPAuZ8cKrqXqKzlyVw_dh-vmCi_s.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\mathrm{A}=\\int_0^4 \\sqrt{4+\\mathrm{y}} \\mathrm{dy}-\\int_0^2 \\sqrt{4-\\mathrm{y}} \\mathrm{dy}-\\int_2^4 \\sqrt{\\mathrm{y}} \\mathrm{dy}$<br/>$=\\left(\\frac{(4+y)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)_0^4+\\left(\\frac{(4-y)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)_0^2-\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right)_0^4$<br/>$\\frac{80 \\sqrt{2}}{3}-16=\\frac{40 \\sqrt{2}}{3}-16$<br/>$\\alpha=6, \\beta=16$<br/>$\\alpha+\\beta=22$",
    "image": null
  },
